From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:17:19 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 74/82] Plutonium: touchpad swipes with three fingers or more
 go to the shell page

libinput's swipe gestures, which the libinput converter didn't read, go on
as ChromeOS's gesture library sends them: scroll events with their finger
count (a fling cancel begins one, a fling start ends it). In shell mode,
Ash's system gesture filter hands those with three fingers or more to a
handler chrome sets, instead of overview and desks: the focused display's
visible shell page gets them as navigator.windowBroker's "touchpadswipe"
event (ShellObserver.OnTouchpadSwipe), {phase, fingers, dx, dy, x, y}.
